# Which portal interfaces a Domicile desktop implements itself.
#
# `xdg-desktop-portal` is the process an application talks to; a desktop
# supplies backends for it to route to, and this file is how it finds one. It
# is read out of `share/xdg-desktop-portal/portals/`, and `UseIn` is matched
# against `XDG_CURRENT_DESKTOP`.
#
# AGAINST THE FRONTEND'S OWN, NOT THE CALLING CLIENT'S, which is the thing to
# know about this file: setting the variable on the clients the compositor
# spawns does nothing for the routing. What reaches the frontend is
# `appearance::say_which_desktop`, which puts the name into the D-Bus and
# systemd activation environments the way every Wayland compositor does at
# startup. A frontend already running under another desktop's name keeps it.
#
# ONE INTERFACE, AND THE REST DELIBERATELY ABSENT. A desktop's backend usually
# implements a dozen: FileChooser, AppChooser, Print, Notification, ScreenCast.
# Domicile implements none of them, and claiming one would take it away from
# whichever backend does -- an interface this file does not name is one the
# frontend routes elsewhere, which is the right answer and the reason this list
# is short rather than aspirational.
#
# Elsewhere is `xdg-desktop-portal-gtk` for most of them. NOT for screenshot or
# screencast, which gtk does not implement either: those are wlroots-protocol
# backends, domicile serves no wlroots protocol, and so a domicile desk has no
# backend for them at all. That is a gap of the desktop rather than of this
# file -- naming the interface here would only move the failure.
#
# `Settings` is here because a theme has to reach the windows. The chrome hears
# about one over the host protocol, and every other window on the desk is a
# Wayland client that has never heard of that socket -- `org.freedesktop.
# appearance`'s `color-scheme` is what GTK4, Qt6, Electron and Firefox all read
# instead. See `packages/domicile-compositor/src/appearance.rs`.
[portal]
DBusName=org.freedesktop.impl.portal.desktop.domicile
Interfaces=org.freedesktop.impl.portal.Settings;
UseIn=domicile
